<title>SPAIN: Beet sugar content at 17.3 pct in southern Spain.</title>
<headline>Beet sugar content at 17.3 pct in southern Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average sugar content of beets in southern Spain was 17.33 percent according to a test conducted on July 13, the National Sugar Beet Confederation CNR told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>The result was slightly up on last year.</p>
<p>The test measured sugar content at the factory gate for the southern harvest from the Andalusian provinces of Cadiz, Seville, Huelva, Cordoba, Jaen, Malaga and Badajoz. The southern harvest began three weeks ago.</p>
<p>The northern harvest begins at the end of September or the beginning of October, and beet tests should be available from early September, the CNR said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34  1 585 2167</p>
</text>
